{"type":"message","id":"84589475","parentId":"d7a8caa8","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:47:51.228Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it. `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py` now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead of `strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\")`. The old format string had nothing to match a trailing `Z`, so it failed on the `Z` suffix. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` pass on Python 3.13.5.\n\nTwo changes in behaviour:\n- **Time zone on `Z` inputs:** a string ending in `Z` now returns a datetime that carries the time zone (UTC). Strings with no zone still return a datetime without one, as before. If code elsewhere compares or subtracts the two kinds, Python raises a `TypeError`. `day_key` is not affected.\n- **Accepts more input:** `fromisoformat` also accepts other ISO-8601 forms, such as fractional seconds, `+02:00`-style offsets and date-only strings, which used to raise an error.\n- **Python version:** reading `Z` with `fromisoformat` needs Python 3.11 or newer. On older versions it would fail on the `Z` again."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":375,"cacheRead":26295,"cacheWrite":431,"totalTokens":27103,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":431}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277266315,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8d8GMyzCDEazSEQLbPv","duration":4911.537096,"ttft":4567.592496000001,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":26728,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
